    "type": "ipmt",
    "ipmt": "# Simplified zoom example based on the murder scenario.\n#\n# Naming is intentionally abstract:\n# - main events: e1, e2, e3\n# - sub-events of e2: e2a1, e2a2, e2a3\n# - deeper sub-event example: e2a3b1\n# - things: t1, t2\n# - concepts: c1, c2, c3, c4\n\ne1\n  --then--\u003e e2\n  --then--\u003e e3\n\ne2 \u003c--::P contains-- e2a1\n  --\u003e c1 ::c\n\ne2 \u003c--::P contains-- e2a2\n  --\u003e c2 ::c\n\ne2 \u003c--::P contains-- e2a3\n  --\u003e c3 ::c\n\ne2a3 \u003c--::P contains-- e2a3b1\ne2a3b1 --\u003e c4 ::c\n\n# Visible inner event order inside e2.\ne2a1 --\u003e e2a2 --\u003e e2a3\n\nt1 ::t\nt2 ::t\n\nt1 ::t --\u003e e2a1, e2a3\n# lifted equals `t2 --\u003e e2a1, e2a2, e2a3, e2a3b1` and `t2 --\u003e e2a1, e2a2, e2a3b1` \nt2 ::t --\u003e e2\n",
